  summary: "Mikhail Gorbachev became leader of the Soviet Communist Party in 1985 and introduced glasnost, or openness, and perestroika, or economic restructuring, in order to reform the Soviet system. The reforms encouraged people to demand more freedom, the communist regimes collapsed one after another, and the 1989 revolutions in Eastern Europe were peaceful everywhere except Romania. The Soviet Union finally disintegrated in 1991 into fifteen sovereign states, ending a Cold War that had started in Europe and could no longer be sustained by a weakening Soviet economy.",
